# The sample PDFs under force-app/idp/examples are generated as plain
# latin1 text with no NUL bytes, so Git's binary auto-detection classifies
# them as text and (with core.autocrlf=true, the Windows default) rewrites
# their LFs to CRLFs on checkout. That shifts every byte offset in the PDF
# xref table and the file stops being a valid PDF. Mark the binary formats
# explicitly so no EOL conversion is ever applied to them.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
